camelRider.description:
{Camel Rider}

{gold|Special Ability : Sand Runner}

Camel Riders increase movement points by 150 on new turn during travelling through sand and dunes terrains.

desertWarrior.description:
{Desert Warrior}

{gold|Special Ability : Sand Runner. Desert Boon}

Desert Warriors increase movement points by 150 on new turn during travelling through sand and dunes terrains.
While fighting on sand and dunes, Desert Warriors gain additional 2 points to Attack, Defense and Speed.

sekhmet.description:
{Priestess}

{gold|Special Ability : Ranged attack. Can cast Cure}

Priestesses can cast Cure three times per battle. This spell heals 25 HP.
Ranged attack is a special ability of creatures, which allows them to attack without engaging into hand-to-hand combat. When attacking in melee, most ranged creatures suffer melee penalty, which halves their damage. Ranged penalty halves the ranged damage farther away than 10 hexes.

sekhmetPriestess.description:
{High Priestess}

{gold|Special Ability : Ranged attack. Can cast Cure}

High Priestesses can cast Cure three times per battle. This spell heals 50 HP.
Ranged attack is a special ability of creatures, which allows them to attack without engaging into hand-to-hand combat. When attacking in melee, most ranged creatures suffer melee penalty, which halves their damage. Ranged penalty halves the ranged damage farther away than 10 hexes.

ammut.description:
{Ammut}

{gold|Special Ability : Blocks Retaliation}

Some creatures have special ability typically phrased as "no enemy retaliation", which does not allow the stack(s) they attack to retaliate against them. This also means, that the attacked stack will not lose one of their retaliations for that combat round if attacked by a creature stack with no enemy retaliation. Thus, while attack with no retaliation is a very strong ability, sometimes it's a double-edged sword as creatures with no enemy retaliation cannot be used to prevent an enemy creature from retaliating that round.

sunAmmut.description:
{Devouring Ammut}

{gold|Special Ability : Life Eater. Blocks Retaliation.}

The devourer grows stronger with each bite! It means Devouring Ammuts gain +3 Maximum Health after every attack. The effect is cumulative.

